  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Liberia: Enhancing People-Centred Justice Service Delivery &#x2013; Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To strengthen, expand, and decentralise transparency and oversight mechanisms within the Judiciary and the Ministry of Justice. 2) To increase citizens&#x2019; understanding of transparency and oversight mechanisms in accessing justice remedies.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: The Judiciary, the Ministry of Justice, the James A.A. Pierre Judiciary Institute, the Judicial Monitoring, Evaluation and Accountability Department (JMEA), and the Prosecution Monitoring Unit (PMU).Indirect beneficiaries: System-level beneficiaries and citizens in select counties.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to improve the efficiency of court operations in order to enhance access to justice and restore public trust in the delivery of justice services.</narrative>
  </description>
